{
    "article_summary": "The article describes an electrochemical method for the direct conversion of free propargylic alcohols into trifluoromethylated allenes. The key innovation is a sodium-mediated pre-association mechanism where Na+ coordinates the alcohol and the trifluoromethyl sulfinate reagent, lowering the energy barrier for the endothermic C-O bond cleavage. This allows for a concerted radical addition pathway under mild conditions, demonstrating broad substrate scope and applicability to late-stage functionalization of pharmaceuticals.",
